<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62794" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεχεποίη</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέχος, ποία</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>grown with grass fit to make a bed</i>, i.e.
				<i>grassy, meadowy</i>, epith. of various towns, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.697
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Ap.</u>
				224
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Merc.</u>
				88
			</span></i>:—masc. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεχεποίης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, of the river
			Asopus, from its grassy banks, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4.383
			</span></i>, Orac. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				9.43
			</span></i>.—<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> has both forms in acc. sg. only; the dat. occurs
		ap.Hdt.l.c.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
